/** @dir Lib/Miro/Reflection
    Reflection and serialization (namespace Miro), included through
    `<Miro/Reflect.h>`.

    - A type is reflectable when it has a reflect(Reflector&) member; the
      MIRO_REFLECT macros write one from a list of fields.
    - toJSON, fromJSON, toJSONString and createFromJSONString (Serialize.h)
      convert to and from JSON; SerializeXml.h is the XML twin.
    - Loading never throws: malformed input or a missing or mistyped field
      leaves that field at its prior value, so check the result where bad
      input matters. Json::parse, by contrast, throws on malformed text.
    - Enums, containers, std::optional, Omittable, std::variant and tagged
      unions are covered by the headers here; Reflector is the visitor every
      serializer and schema walker implements.
*/
